# ConfirmAgentPlan.srv - Trusted internal binding after exact plan presentation.
# NOT a way to grant or modify authorize_motion.
#
# See docs/lightweight_skill_package_registry_design_zh.md section 11.6.
#
# The Agent must first generate a fresh task_id and present the user with the
# plan kind, ordered steps, typed parameters, exact snapshot identity and that
# task_id and synchronously flush that presentation; the CLI then calls this
# service immediately without a second user confirmation gate.
# The coordinator/plan store must atomically validate
# (plan_token, plan_digest, task_id, registry_epoch, registry_generation,
# registry_digest, task_budget_sec), transition the plan from VALIDATED to
# CONFIRMED and return a single-use confirmation_token bound to that exact
# tuple. Mismatch, duplicate
# confirmation, expired plan or reload-changed identity all fail closed.
#
# execution_mode must match the mode captured by PlanAgentCommand. The
# immediate mode removes only the user confirmation wait; all Gateway and
# operator authorization checks remain mandatory. confirmation_token does not grant motion authorization, does not hold the
# root lease and does not enter any digest; it only proves that this exact
# plan/task pair has been bound once. schema_version is 1 in v1.

uint32 schema_version
string plan_token
string plan_digest
string task_id
string registry_epoch
uint64 registry_generation
string registry_digest
float32 task_budget_sec
string execution_mode
---
bool confirmed
string confirmation_token
float32 confirmed_task_budget_sec
builtin_interfaces/Time task_budget_started_at
builtin_interfaces/Time task_budget_deadline
string error_code
string message
SkillDiagnostic[] diagnostics
